<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Premier has govt approval for bid.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Premier has govt approval for bid.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.K.-based Premier Oil Plc said on Monday it had received approval from the Australian government's Foreign Investment Review Board to proceed with its takeover offer for Discovery Petroleum NL.</p>
<p>Premier last week raised its offer for Discovery to 80 cents a share from 70 cents, increasing the value of its offer to A$104.2 million from A$91.9 million.</p>
<p>Discovery has yet to endorse the higher offer. Premier is seeking a minimum of 50.1 percent control, with the bid set to close on December 11. Discovery shares were trading at 81 cents on Monday on heavy turnover.- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
